LoudKit includes local text-to-speech and voice enrollment functionality.
A user can create a reusable voice profile from a recording and synthesize new
speech with it. This is intended for voices the user owns or has permission to
use, including accessibility, localization, product speech and creative work.

The same capability can be misused for impersonation or deceptive synthetic
media. Users are responsible for obtaining consent, disclosing synthetic audio
where appropriate and following applicable law. LoudKit does not provide voice
authentication bypasses or tools for removing provenance metadata.

The project's full responsible-use policy is available at:
https://github.com/loudreader/loudkit/blob/main/RESPONSIBLE_USE.md
